This process explain that how to setup Prometheus and Grafana  for Pods in Kops K8s Cluster
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Create Kops cluster : multi node cluster
#sh kopscluster.sh
------------------------------------------
Generally all the cluster related data store on local machine but what if something goes wrong with local machine - all data gone
Store cluster entire information at s3 so create a bucket and enable versioning for backup
#sh s3-cluster-state.sh
note: must change bucket name in file
-----------------------------------------
Install Helm : package manager for K8s used to download applicaion in k8s cluster
#sh helm.sh
-----------------------------------------
Install Metric-Server : Metric Server will collect the memory and cpu metric from kubelet and expose them through K8s Metric API
#sh metric-server-sh
-----------------------------------------

============================================
SETUP AND INSTALL PROMETHEUS AND GRAGANA NOW
============================================

Add prometheus and grafana chart to helm repo -----
#sh add-PG.sh

CREATE PROMETHEUS NAMESPACE AND INSTALL PROMETHEUS HERE
======================================================
#kubectl create ns prometheus
#sh prometheus.sh
#kubectl get all -n prometheus

Note: commands already present in file if you create ns manually remove line in file or just run ===prometheus.sh===

CREATE GRAFANA NAMESPACE AND INSTALL GRAFANA HERE
=================================================
#kubectl create na grafana
#sh grafana.sh
#kubectl get ll -n grafana

Note: commands already present in file if you create ns manually remove line in file or just run ===grafana.sh===

In grafana.sh -- we expose the service through LoadBlancer - take LB DNS-name put it in browser to access Grafana
=========================================================
username=admin
adminPassword=Root123456
========================================================

Note: since grafana namespace is separate from prometheus, you'll need to connect Grafana to Prometheus as a data source
---flow
grafana dashboard --> add the data source --> select prometheus --> paste url- 
||http://prometheus-server.prometheus.svc.cluster.local|| --> save & test


Import Grafana Dashboard to visualize data into graphs and monitor Pods and Cluster
---flow
dashboard --> new --> import --> 6417  --> load --> select prometheus --> import

